  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2>ByteSIM Promo Code FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>What is the best code right now</h3>
      <p><strong>TPDBYTE</strong>. It's advertised as 10% off, but we tested it on a real order and it only saved about 5%, similar to ByteSIM's automatic Summer Sale.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does ByteSIM give you a real phone number</h3>
      <p>Yes, in select countries including the US, Canada, UK, France, Spain, Australia, Vietnam, South Korea, and Thailand. Plans with a number bundle in calls, texts, hotspot sharing, and a local IP address alongside data.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Do I need to verify my identity to use ByteSIM</h3>
      <p>Only for local-number plans, per local telecom regulation; most data-only ByteSIM eSIMs don't require it. A number plan means uploading a passport photo and a selfie.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>What happens if activation doesn't work right away</h3>
      <p>In our own test, the eSIM didn't come online right after identity verification. ByteSIM's WhatsApp support connected us with a real person within minutes, who explained it can take 2 to 10 minutes after verification and that billing only starts once you actually tap activate. It still wasn't showing as active after that, and what actually fixed it was support checking back in on their own, unprompted, about two hours later.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>When does a ByteSIM plan start billing</h3>
      <p>Only after you tap activate, per ByteSIM's own support. You can complete identity verification and let the eSIM sit installed without it counting against your plan until you actually turn it on.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

